    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.Title">Welcome!</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.Text">This is the first launch of the ModAPI. Before you can start you have to check the following options:</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.AutoUpdate">Auto-update</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.AutoUpdateText">If you enable the auto-update function you will get informed when there is a new version of the ModAPI available. If there is a new update you can simply apply the new update with 1-click.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.Steam">Steam connection</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.SteamText">The steam connection allows you to access steam functions in-game (e.g. Steam overlay). The ModAPI will also be able to restore your game files if they get corrupted or modified.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.UpdateVersions">Update VersionsData table</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.UpdateVersionsText">When you activate the VersionsData table update the ModAPI will download the VersionsData table on start. This means new updates of the game will be recognized by the ModAPI automaticlly without updating it manually. It can take up to 24 hours before new VersionsData are added to the VersionsData table.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.FirstSetup.Buttons.Confirm">Continue</s:String>


    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.UpdateAvailable.Title">Update available!</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.UpdateAvailable.Text">There is a new version for the ModAPI. Do you want to update now?</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.UpdateAvailable.Buttons.Update">Update now</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="Lang.Windows.UpdateAvailable.Buttons.Later">Update later</s:String>


